{{-- Pre-paint auth bounce.

     A plain script, not a client block: it has to run before anything paints
     and before the runtime exists, or a signed-out visitor sees the app shell
     first and then gets thrown out of it.

     **The server decides, not this script.** It used to look for the session
     cookie in `document.cookie`, which cannot work: the framework sets that
     cookie `HttpOnly`, so a page script never sees it no matter who is signed
     in. Every authenticated visitor was therefore bounced to /login, and
     signing in produced a redirect loop between the two pages. It went
     unnoticed for a long time because curl does not run scripts, so every page
     returned 200 with correct markup while being unusable in a browser.

     So the page renders `#auth-required` when the server could not identify the
     visitor, and `#auth-pending` when a cookie was presented and did not
     authenticate. The first says where to go; the second says to bin the stale
     cookie on the way, which is what stops an expired token from bouncing
     somebody back and forth forever. --}}
<script>
(function () {
  if (!document.getElementById('auth-required')) return

  if (document.getElementById('auth-pending')) {
    var name = document.documentElement.getAttribute('data-session-cookie') || 'auth-token'
    // Best effort: an HttpOnly cookie cannot be cleared from here either, and
    // the server clears it on the next response. This only catches a
    // non-HttpOnly copy left by an older session.
    document.cookie = name + '=; path=/; max-age=0'
  }

  window.location.replace('/login')
}())
</script>
